.Dd November 19, 2026
.Dt RUN-NV-VULKAN.SH 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm run-nv-vulkan.sh
.Nd run the Linux aarch64 Vulkan stack against the NVIDIA card
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm vulkaninfo
.Op Ar options
.Nm
.Cm list
.Op Ar options
.Nm
.Cm bench
.Op Ar model.gguf
.Op Ar options
.Nm
.Cm server
.Ar model
.Op Ar options
.Nm
.Cm llama-bench
.Op Ar options
.Nm
.Cm rpc
.Op Ar options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs the Linux aarch64 Vulkan userspace against the NVIDIA card through the
Linuxulator.
The programs are started from private Linux roots of their own; nothing in
.Pa /compat/linux
is touched.
.Pp
The modes are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm vulkaninfo
The Rocky Vulkan loader and
.Xr vulkaninfo 1
against the ICD.
It runs
.Cm vulkaninfo --summary
when it is given no options of its own; the options it is given are passed
on instead of
.Fl -summary .
.It Cm list
.Xr llama-bench 1
.Fl -list-devices ,
with the options after it.
.It Cm bench
.Xr llama-bench 1
with one model, prompt 512 and 128 tokens, every layer on the GPU and flash
attention off and on.
The options that follow the model are passed on to
.Xr llama-bench 1 .
.It Cm server
.Xr llama-server 1
with one model and the given options.
.It Cm llama-bench
.Xr llama-bench 1
with the given options; no model is added, the model is yours to pass, as an
absolute path.
.It Cm rpc
.Xr ggml-rpc-server 1
with the given options.
.El
.Pp
Only
.Cm bench
and
.Cm server
take a model.
In the other modes the second argument is one of the program's own options and
is passed on unchanged.
An empty model argument is a missing argument, not the default model:
.Cm bench \(dq\(dq
and
.Cm server \(dq\(dq
stop with exit 2.
.Pp
.Xr llama-bench 1
appends the flags
.Cm -m
.Cm -p
.Cm -n
.Cm -ngl
and
.Cm -fa
to a list: a flag given twice does not override the first one, it adds a
second run.
The defaults of
.Cm bench
.Cm -p 512
.Cm -n 128
.Cm -ngl 99
and
.Cm -fa 0,1
are therefore added only for the flags your options do not give themselves,
and a
.Cm -m
in the options of
.Cm bench
or
.Cm server
is refused (exit 2), by its short or long name:
the model is that mode's own argument.
llama-bench would run both models, and llama-server would silently use the last one.
The defaults of
.Cm bench
are likewise added only when neither the short nor the long name of the flag is given.
.Pp
The
.Cm -fa 0,1
default is what makes the rows comparable: the default flash attention of
.Xr llama-bench 1
is AUTO, it writes that as
.Cm -1 ,
and a
.Cm -1
row matches no published
.Cm fa
0 or
.Cm fa
1 row.
.Pp
Every mode runs from the llama directory, because ggml finds its backends next
to the executable and in the current directory, and the executable here is
.Pa ld-linux-aarch64.so.1
from the Ubuntu root, so only the current-directory search finds them.
A relative path in the options is therefore relative to that directory: pass
absolute ones.
The model path itself is made absolute against the directory the script was
started from.
.Pp
The NVIDIA Vulkan ICD starts through libEGL (glvnd).
Without the EGL vendor file libEGL finds no NVIDIA vendor and the loader
says "Could not get 'vkCreateInstance' via 'vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr' for
ICD libGLX_nvidia.so.0" and "Found no drivers!".
The function
.Fn vk_icdGetInstanceProcAddr
returns NULL in that case.
Any launcher that does not use this script has to set both variables itself.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "GB10_WORK"
.It Ev GB10_WORK
The work root.
The default is the
.Pa work/
directory of the checkout;
.Ev GB10_WORK
overrides it.
It holds:
.Bl -tag -width "linuxroot/nv/" -compact
.It Pa linuxroot/nv/
NVIDIA's user libraries, the Vulkan ICD file
.Pa nvidia_icd.json
and the EGL vendor file
.Pa 10_nvidia.json .
.It Pa linuxroot/rl9/
Rocky 9: Vulkan loader,
.Xr vulkaninfo 1 ,
libglvnd, the X11, xcb and Wayland client libraries, libffi.
.It Pa linuxroot/noble/
Ubuntu 24.04: glibc, libstdc++, libgomp, Vulkan loader,
.Xr vulkaninfo 1 ,
the X11/glvnd libraries: what the official llama.cpp
.Pa ubuntu-vulkan-arm64
build needs.
.It Pa llm/llama-vulkan-arm64/llama-b12531/
The llama.cpp build.
.El
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
The command ran.
.It 1
A path is missing.
.It 2
An unknown mode, a missing argument, or an option the mode does not take.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Run
.Xr llama-bench 1
to list the devices:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ run-nv-vulkan.sh list
.Ed
.Pp
Benchmark one model with the defaults (prompt 512, 128 tokens, every layer on
the GPU, flash attention off and on):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ run-nv-vulkan.sh bench /path/to/models/Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf
.Ed
.Pp
Benchmark one model with a longer prompt and a longer generation; the
.Cm -p
and
.Cm -n
defaults are not added, because they were given:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ run-nv-vulkan.sh bench model.gguf -p 1024 -n 256
.Ed
.Pp
Serve one model:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ run-nv-vulkan.sh server /path/to/models/Llama-3.2-3B-Instruct-Q4_K_M.gguf --port 18080
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ggml-rpc-server 1 ,
.Xr llama-bench 1 ,
.Xr llama-server 1 ,
.Xr vulkaninfo 1
.Sh CAVEATS
The Vulkan loader and the ICD are the Linux ones, run through the
Linuxulator; the driver on the FreeBSD side is what has to be right.
